    Bug 1941495 - Attempt to fix intermittent fail in browser_ext_contentScripts.js. r=mkmelin

    The intermittent occurs when injecting takes longer than the expected
    max delay of 500ms currently used in `checkContent()`. This seems to be
    an issue specifically for injection caused by a manifest entry right
    after the extension was loaded.

    To generate a usable event to listen for a successful injection, the
    patch adds a notification at the end of each injected script.

    The first 3 CSS-only tests are not able to generate this event, but
    have so far not been observed to fail intermittently.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D239869

